; ted-freeupa5-allocnull-dangling (#361): freeupa5 on the only line of
; the text makes a new empty line with afirst2 and frees the old line
; whether that allocation worked or not: with allocnull failing,
; firstitem, enditem and thisitem point at the freed line.  TED alone
; under inject (alerts answered): lines "a" and "b"; block over the whole
; first line (F1 at its start, F2 at the start of line 2), Join (the
; block stays on line 1, which is now the only line), Block Kill (the
; whole only line: freeupa5's .freeonly); the 4th AllocMem of 10 bytes
; (MEMF_PUBLIC) of TED's process, that allocnull, fails (the first three
; are made at the start, the third by the allocnull of the start's
; donew).  SAVE, QUIT.
; Correct (the fix of the issue): the alert "Not enough memory for
; operation!", the line stays and is saved as it is; the original frees
; it and saves what the freed memory holds then (or crashes).
; @fixed #361
; @file bo.bas "a\nb"
; @source F bo.bas
; @command TEDAB:tools/inject alerts allocfail=10-10/f=1/1+3 blitz2:ted @FILE@
; @expect stdout "inject: allocfail: 1 allocations failed"
; @expect stdout "inject: alert: Not enough memory for operation!"
; @expect data bo.bas "ab\n"
timeout 20
wait screen
key 50
key 4d
key 51
key 4c
menu 1 8
menu 1 1
wait screen
menu 0 2
wait freq "Name to save file as"
freq ok
wait screen
menu 0 9
wait exit
